1
00:02:04,187 --> 00:02:08,187
A long, long time ago
in the splendid East,

2
00:02:09,687 --> 00:02:13,103
People toiled at dawn
and rested at dusk.

3
00:02:13,104 --> 00:02:15,812
Life was filled with
peace and happiness.

4
00:02:17,354 --> 00:02:22,979
However, at the end of each
year, they'd go into Hiding.

5
00:02:28,854 --> 00:02:33,354
I'm the year monster.
Feed me your naughty Kids.

6
00:02:38,396 --> 00:02:39,646
Not so fast.

7
00:02:43,771 --> 00:02:46,021
Who should I eat first?

8
00:02:47,396 --> 00:02:50,062
Maybe I'll just swallow you all.

9
00:02:50,104 --> 00:02:51,104
Stop that.

10
00:02:52,229 --> 00:02:54,521
On the horizon, a
warrior appeared.

11
00:02:55,104 --> 00:02:57,896
Don't be scared. I
know his weakness.

12
00:02:58,062 --> 00:02:59,729
He's afraid of red.

13
00:02:59,771 --> 00:03:01,229
Red. Yes.

14
00:03:02,062 --> 00:03:03,979
You've got to be kidding me.

15
00:03:07,896 --> 00:03:10,979
Red lanterns in your Face.

16
00:03:14,562 --> 00:03:17,479
Next up, couplets.

17
00:03:21,937 --> 00:03:24,854
And finally...

18
00:03:25,021 --> 00:03:27,729
Firecrackers. My arch enemies.

19
00:03:28,812 --> 00:03:30,354
Let's light this up.

20
00:03:33,396 --> 00:03:35,437
I'll be back next year.

21
00:03:40,187 --> 00:03:43,729
Ever since then, at the end
of the year, people gather

22
00:03:43,771 --> 00:03:47,979
Together to hang couplets,
hand out red packets,

23
00:03:48,021 --> 00:03:50,104
And set off fireworks.

24
00:03:51,812 --> 00:03:56,146
As the years went by, these
became our New Year Traditions.

25
00:03:56,187 --> 00:03:59,437
(The Hidden Protector)

26
00:04:18,729 --> 00:04:21,146
Oh, yeah.

27
00:04:21,187 --> 00:04:21,646
Briar.

28
00:04:24,896 --> 00:04:25,312
Yeah.

29
00:04:28,604 --> 00:04:28,771
Yeah.

30
00:04:33,271 --> 00:04:33,812
That's better.

31
00:04:36,271 --> 00:04:38,021
We'll make it through
the winter with Briar here.

32
00:04:38,229 --> 00:04:39,729
Briar, you're the best.

33
00:04:48,646 --> 00:04:49,229
Yeah.

34
00:05:01,312 --> 00:05:01,979
Wow, Briar, you're so strong.

35
00:05:03,521 --> 00:05:05,312
What a catchy tune. Oh.

36
00:05:06,437 --> 00:05:08,271
Briar, you're making us proud.

37
00:05:11,562 --> 00:05:12,312
Boo.

38
00:05:12,854 --> 00:05:16,104
That snow needs
clearing. And over there.

39
00:05:27,937 --> 00:05:31,604
Briar, you said we'd celebrate
the new year together.

40
00:05:31,771 --> 00:05:35,521
Come on. Imagine,
dumplings, couplets,

41
00:05:35,562 --> 00:05:39,521
Firecrackers, funny, and
so many other fun things.

42
00:05:40,187 --> 00:05:41,229
I can't.

43
00:05:42,896 --> 00:05:43,521
Why not?

44
00:05:44,396 --> 00:05:48,436
Tell me this, do animals
celebrate New Year? Can you tell?

45
00:05:48,437 --> 00:05:50,979
Never. The only way
we'll show up is on a plate.

46
00:05:54,771 --> 00:05:58,687
Second, our homes are
buried. There's no time to play.

47
00:05:58,896 --> 00:06:02,020
If I don't help our friends,
they won't have a place to stay.

48
00:06:02,021 --> 00:06:05,812
But Briar, I'm sure they'll
be just fine without you.

49
00:06:05,854 --> 00:06:08,312
You can't be all
work and no play.

50
00:06:08,354 --> 00:06:13,020
Huh? No play? It's a big project.
What if something goes Wrong?

51
00:06:13,021 --> 00:06:15,021
I won't leave until it's done.

52
00:06:15,521 --> 00:06:16,771
Oh, what could go wrong?

53
00:06:16,937 --> 00:06:18,104
Would you shut your snapper?

54
00:06:19,104 --> 00:06:21,479
Now go throw these away. Go.

55
00:06:21,604 --> 00:06:24,062
It's not fun, but
it has to be done.

56
00:06:24,396 --> 00:06:25,979
Is there anything
else we can help with?

57
00:06:26,687 --> 00:06:27,396
Go help Tikky

58
00:06:28,812 --> 00:06:31,979
(25 days left)

59
00:06:34,771 --> 00:06:38,228
We're animals. We don't
have fun. Briar promised

60
00:06:38,229 --> 00:06:40,895
he'd Celebrate the New
Year holiday with me.

61
00:06:40,896 --> 00:06:45,770
But he broke his word.
I'm sorry, little Firework.

62
00:06:45,771 --> 00:06:48,771
I have to throw you away.

63
00:06:52,521 --> 00:06:55,729
I just want to have some fun.
What's so wrong about that?

64
00:06:57,896 --> 00:06:58,479
Go away.

65
00:06:59,437 --> 00:07:03,354
I said beat me... alone?

66
00:07:11,854 --> 00:07:13,854
Are you a monster?

67
00:07:14,521 --> 00:07:15,562
Me?

68
00:07:16,437 --> 00:07:20,396
You're facing the one
who snacks on little kids.

69
00:07:20,479 --> 00:07:22,771
The beast who even adults fear.

70
00:07:23,604 --> 00:07:25,854
The Year Monster.

71
00:07:28,021 --> 00:07:30,479
Is that really you?

72
00:07:30,521 --> 00:07:32,937
In the flesh.

73
00:07:33,271 --> 00:07:34,937
Go away.

74
00:07:34,979 --> 00:07:41,312
So many red things. I'm
done for. Growing weak.

75
00:07:41,771 --> 00:07:44,187
Really? It worked?

76
00:07:44,937 --> 00:07:47,312
Gotcha.

77
00:07:49,896 --> 00:07:54,896
Believe it or not, red is
actually my favorite Color.

78
00:07:57,604 --> 00:08:01,062
Firework. How do you like that?
I just need something to light it.

79
00:08:01,146 --> 00:08:02,145
Here

80
00:08:02,146 --> 00:08:04,562
Oh, yeah. Thanks.
That's very kind of you.

81
00:08:20,646 --> 00:08:23,187
Fire!

82
00:08:23,229 --> 00:08:23,896
Tasty.

83
00:08:24,771 --> 00:08:28,396
So let me guess, that flavor
was dragon's breath, right?

84
00:08:28,646 --> 00:08:29,521
Oh.

85
00:08:34,937 --> 00:08:37,729
Is this a running club?
Do you want a Drink?

86
00:08:38,479 --> 00:08:40,896
Briar, help me!

87
00:08:44,979 --> 00:08:46,437
Just relax.

88
00:08:47,771 --> 00:08:49,396
You need my help.

89
00:08:49,437 --> 00:08:51,812
Huh? You want to help me?

90
00:08:51,979 --> 00:08:54,187
That's right. I
heard everything.

91
00:08:54,521 --> 00:08:57,937
All you want is a little
New Year fun, right?

92
00:08:58,687 --> 00:08:59,146
Yeah.

93
00:08:59,896 --> 00:09:02,229
You aren't asking for much, but

94
00:09:03,396 --> 00:09:05,271
Because of your
brother's nonsense,

95
00:09:06,354 --> 00:09:08,229
The other animals
won't celebrate.

96
00:09:09,646 --> 00:09:12,896
And you're all on your
own with no one to play with.

97
00:09:13,396 --> 00:09:14,354
So sad,

98
00:09:14,771 --> 00:09:16,146
So lonely.

99
00:09:18,312 --> 00:09:21,812
Is this supposed to be
me? You forgot my muscles.

100
00:09:25,396 --> 00:09:30,770
Anyway, you should make a pact
with me, then you'll inherit my Powers,

101
00:09:30,771 --> 00:09:33,896
and you can have
whatever you want.

102
00:09:37,354 --> 00:09:42,229
Well, what do you think? Is
this fancy villa to your liking?

103
00:09:42,312 --> 00:09:44,562
If not- ...

104
00:09:44,604 --> 00:09:48,354
How about your own
private theme park?

105
00:09:53,562 --> 00:09:54,979
(Bram Vomiting)

106
00:09:55,979 --> 00:09:59,937
Well, what do you think?
Place your paw print here to

107
00:09:59,979 --> 00:10:02,354
Inherit the Year
Monster's powers.

108
00:10:03,271 --> 00:10:07,812
Then, whatever
you want is yours.

109
00:10:11,562 --> 00:10:13,937
Briar, we're headed
home. Good night, Briar.

110
00:10:14,229 --> 00:10:16,771
Good night. Sleep tight,
everyone. Great job.

111
00:10:16,896 --> 00:10:20,436
See you tomorrow. Let's go home

112
00:10:20,437 --> 00:10:21,729
Hey, Vick.

113
00:10:22,562 --> 00:10:23,646
Thanks for today.

114
00:10:24,937 --> 00:10:26,854
No need to be so
formal. We're friends.

115
00:10:26,937 --> 00:10:29,771
Huh. You're spending
New Year's here?

116
00:10:30,729 --> 00:10:33,646
Looks like it. My parents
expect a girlfriend.

117
00:10:33,979 --> 00:10:37,812
I don't want to disappoint them. I'd rather
spend New Year's here with you guys.

118
00:10:37,937 --> 00:10:40,853
Hmm. Humans are complex.

119
00:10:40,854 --> 00:10:41,896
All right.

120
00:10:42,812 --> 00:10:45,937
Oh, I smell pretty awful.
Guess it's time for a shower.

121
00:10:46,021 --> 00:10:46,521
Enjoy.

122
00:10:49,812 --> 00:10:50,562
What's that?

123
00:10:52,437 --> 00:10:53,271
Bram!

124
00:11:07,396 --> 00:11:09,896
What's going on?

125
00:11:24,187 --> 00:11:25,104
Bramble!

126
00:11:29,354 --> 00:11:31,854
Wait for Me.

127
00:12:13,104 --> 00:12:14,854
(laughter)

128
00:12:14,937 --> 00:12:17,771
Yes! I'm finally free.

129
00:12:18,104 --> 00:12:19,229
Huh?

130
00:12:20,521 --> 00:12:23,646
Now it's up to
you guys. Bye bye.

131
00:12:27,187 --> 00:12:30,854
Bramble. Who's she?
Bramble, your head.

132
00:12:30,937 --> 00:12:31,521
Huh?

133
00:12:34,062 --> 00:12:34,437
Hey.

134
00:12:34,604 --> 00:12:35,729
What are those?

135
00:12:35,979 --> 00:12:36,979
(Vic Grunts)

136
00:12:37,229 --> 00:12:38,521
Itchy.

137
00:12:39,271 --> 00:12:40,062
So itchy.

138
00:12:41,979 --> 00:12:45,229
Briar, Bramble,
are you guys okay?

139
00:12:47,687 --> 00:12:48,771
And who is that?

140
00:12:48,937 --> 00:12:50,729
Vic, you got hair.

141
00:12:51,812 --> 00:12:54,521
I have hair now?

142
00:12:55,729 --> 00:12:57,021
I really have hair.

143
00:12:57,062 --> 00:12:57,896
Five-ball Vic.

144
00:12:59,021 --> 00:13:01,604
Look, I got antlers. They're
sticking out of my head.

145
00:13:02,021 --> 00:13:03,479
Oh, let me touch them.

146
00:13:03,687 --> 00:13:04,229
What's happening?

147
00:13:04,271 --> 00:13:04,812
Here, touch my hair.

148
00:13:04,854 --> 00:13:07,479
Bro, you got to come
feel this. It's so fluffy.

149
00:13:07,646 --> 00:13:08,979
It's just like a little lamb.

150
00:13:10,187 --> 00:13:11,062
Let me try.

151
00:13:11,979 --> 00:13:15,354
Wait, that's not the point.
Bram, what was that?

152
00:13:16,229 --> 00:13:19,229
Well, that, it was...

153
00:13:33,312 --> 00:13:35,437
What? What.... what's that?

154
00:13:35,479 --> 00:13:36,771
Oh,

155
00:13:52,146 --> 00:13:53,979
Freezing.

156
00:14:07,437 --> 00:14:08,354
Take them.

157
00:14:13,854 --> 00:14:15,728
Briar, I'm scared.

158
00:14:15,729 --> 00:14:17,396
Don't be. I'll keep you safe.

159
00:14:35,729 --> 00:14:37,854
(Electric shock)

160
00:14:40,271 --> 00:14:40,729
Briar.

161
00:14:43,021 --> 00:14:45,521
Briar, say something.

162
00:15:08,729 --> 00:15:11,479
Who are these people?

163
00:15:12,271 --> 00:15:13,562
Where do they get their power?

164
00:15:13,771 --> 00:15:16,979
If I knew we were going, I would've
brought some snacks or something.

165
00:15:17,104 --> 00:15:19,479
Ah, I'm starving.

166
00:15:19,604 --> 00:15:21,186
Oh, come on.

167
00:15:21,187 --> 00:15:24,604
They messed up my
curly mane. Not you.

168
00:15:24,937 --> 00:15:27,312
Greetings, valued guests.

169
00:15:30,146 --> 00:15:32,687
Did his voice totally
change or is it just me?

170
00:15:34,937 --> 00:15:35,479
Ta-da.

171
00:15:37,437 --> 00:15:38,812
The voice you just heard

172
00:15:39,771 --> 00:15:41,437
Was yours truly.

173
00:15:42,437 --> 00:15:46,146
Sorry about your welcome.
Don't get us wrong,

174
00:15:46,521 --> 00:15:49,437
We're actually the nice guys.

175
00:15:50,854 --> 00:15:54,812
Come now, Robin. I've told
you before, that grim face will

176
00:15:54,896 --> 00:15:57,354
Scare all the kids. Watch me.

177
00:15:57,396 --> 00:15:59,271
Big Smile.

178
00:16:04,271 --> 00:16:07,229
Mommy, I want to go home.

179
00:16:09,771 --> 00:16:10,562
We'll work on it.

180
00:16:11,271 --> 00:16:12,771
Where is the ship headed?

181
00:16:13,479 --> 00:16:16,937
To a hidden realm where ordinary

182
00:16:17,062 --> 00:16:19,729
Souls cannot reach.

183
00:16:19,771 --> 00:16:22,562
People, Behold.

184
00:16:31,521 --> 00:16:33,104
Whoa.

185
00:16:40,021 --> 00:16:43,729
Think we're going to crash.

186
00:16:58,521 --> 00:16:59,729
What?

187
00:16:59,771 --> 00:17:01,021
What is this place?

188
00:17:03,479 --> 00:17:07,479
It says something Eve?

189
00:17:07,896 --> 00:17:09,896
Can't you read the plaque?

190
00:17:22,729 --> 00:17:25,729
Welcome to Eve City.

191
00:17:26,729 --> 00:17:30,646
About 4,000 years
ago, our ancestors

192
00:17:30,729 --> 00:17:33,561
Followed the Year
Monster and settled here.

193
00:17:33,562 --> 00:17:35,896
As time passed,
the city expanded.

194
00:17:37,146 --> 00:17:40,896
Thanks to this realm's unique
resources, we've developed our

195
00:17:40,979 --> 00:17:43,062
Own technology and culture.

196
00:17:52,521 --> 00:17:56,396
Some of the residents
gained supernatural powers,

197
00:17:56,437 --> 00:17:59,437
Elemental powers to be specific.

198
00:18:00,396 --> 00:18:02,729
Yeah. Battery trouble.

199
00:18:03,604 --> 00:18:04,729
Whoa.

200
00:18:11,021 --> 00:18:14,229
But what about this place?

201
00:18:18,771 --> 00:18:21,771
This is the restricted zone and

202
00:18:21,896 --> 00:18:24,187
Prison of Sha.

203
00:18:25,146 --> 00:18:26,646
The prison sharks?

204
00:18:26,771 --> 00:18:28,604
Just Sha. No arcs.

205
00:18:30,771 --> 00:18:31,354
Sha?

206
00:18:32,229 --> 00:18:33,271
You failed school, didn't you?

207
00:18:34,187 --> 00:18:34,604
Mm-hmm.

208
00:18:34,646 --> 00:18:35,854
Didn't go.

209
00:18:36,646 --> 00:18:40,354
At the beginning of time, the
Year Monster and Sha were born.

210
00:18:41,062 --> 00:18:45,812
They were like fire and ice,
natural enemies fighting for Eternity.

211
00:18:45,854 --> 00:18:48,686
Sha brought his army
of minions to torment

212
00:18:48,687 --> 00:18:52,187
The human world. Where
they went, suffering followed.

213
00:18:52,521 --> 00:18:56,854
Thankfully, the Year Monster
and her followers rose up and finally

214
00:18:56,896 --> 00:19:00,271
Subdued Sha. Nevertheless,

215
00:19:00,312 --> 00:19:05,771
he can't Be killed! That's why
the Year Monster's followers

216
00:19:05,896 --> 00:19:07,812
built this very prison,

217
00:19:07,854 --> 00:19:11,229
and Sha was sealed within it.

218
00:19:18,687 --> 00:19:20,604
Ahh...

219
00:19:31,104 --> 00:19:33,396
What happens if he breaks free?

220
00:19:33,812 --> 00:19:35,646
The end of days.

221
00:19:36,479 --> 00:19:39,729
Worldwide demise.

222
00:19:40,437 --> 00:19:43,187
Don't scare them
like that. Relax.

223
00:19:43,479 --> 00:19:47,396
Every New Year's Eve, the brave
lady of Eve City will take action.

224
00:19:47,729 --> 00:19:51,146
With the help of the Armula,
she amplifies her power,

225
00:19:51,562 --> 00:19:54,270
Driving Sha back into the seal.

226
00:19:54,271 --> 00:19:58,145
Shoom, Bang, boom.
Our almighty hero,

227
00:19:58,146 --> 00:20:01,437
the Year Monster, saves
the world once again.

228
00:20:01,479 --> 00:20:03,771
Wait a sec. I know
that bamboozler.

229
00:20:03,896 --> 00:20:06,854
Not her. The one you
met was Lady Nian.

230
00:20:07,812 --> 00:20:11,437
This is her twin, Lady Sui,
in the blue, her twin sister.

231
00:20:12,229 --> 00:20:13,396
Oh, I see.

232
00:20:13,771 --> 00:20:16,187
I always thought that
the Year Monster was evil.

233
00:20:16,396 --> 00:20:17,812
But she's no monster.

234
00:20:17,896 --> 00:20:21,354
Hang on a sec. What does
that have to do with us?

235
00:20:22,021 --> 00:20:25,437
Everything and more. You
have Lady Nian's powers,

236
00:20:25,479 --> 00:20:29,104
so this year, you
three will seal away Sha

237
00:20:29,646 --> 00:20:31,229
Huh?

238
00:20:35,979 --> 00:20:37,646
Goldman, plug in port 10.

239
00:20:38,437 --> 00:20:40,646
Port 10 connected.
Calibrating now.

240
00:20:41,229 --> 00:20:43,687
Energy frequency is
syncing with output.

241
00:20:44,229 --> 00:20:47,687
Port three, port
four. That's it!

242
00:20:47,854 --> 00:20:48,771
I Finally did it.

243
00:20:48,896 --> 00:20:49,979
Ramsey.

244
00:20:52,312 --> 00:20:53,187
General Robin!

245
00:20:53,271 --> 00:20:55,854
Is that how you
guard the library?

246
00:20:55,896 --> 00:20:59,396
By handing out
the secret scroll?

247
00:21:00,187 --> 00:21:02,104
I don't know.

248
00:21:03,646 --> 00:21:05,812
You put Ramsey down now!

249
00:21:09,479 --> 00:21:13,271
Unhand that poor boy.
I just... It's his assistant.

250
00:21:13,312 --> 00:21:15,146
He's doing us a
favor by being here.

251
00:21:15,812 --> 00:21:18,729
General, don't lose
your temper this time.

252
00:21:19,937 --> 00:21:22,562
Goldman, Silver,
help me talk him down.

253
00:21:22,687 --> 00:21:26,021
General, it's true. He's been
working on the Armula with us

254
00:21:26,187 --> 00:21:27,937
Non-stop for three days.

255
00:21:28,771 --> 00:21:29,771
Did you hear what he said?

256
00:21:29,854 --> 00:21:31,812
Yeah, I did. Three
days of overtime.

257
00:21:32,021 --> 00:21:35,854
No, not that. He said the only ones
who can seal the evil monster are you.

258
00:21:35,979 --> 00:21:38,937
Maybe this is a
new type of scam.

259
00:21:38,979 --> 00:21:41,187
I say we give the
powers back to them.

260
00:21:41,229 --> 00:21:42,146
Wait a minute.

261
00:21:42,646 --> 00:21:43,771
Oh, no!

262
00:21:43,812 --> 00:21:47,937
Excuse me. If we return the Year
Monster's powers, can I keep my Hair?

263
00:21:47,979 --> 00:21:48,771
Of course not.

264
00:21:48,812 --> 00:21:49,353
Gotcha.

265
00:21:49,354 --> 00:21:50,854
Back Uncle.

